Amplifier bus diagnosis: SDA/SCL pad levels and the always-powered chips on SE1.

All chips NACKed with the pins already on qup1 (all12, all13), the LED driver too. The live DT
puts the max77729 charger/fuel gauge (0x66) and sc8551 charger (0x65) on the same bus; both run
off the battery, so they tell a dead bus from unpowered amplifiers. The pad levels of GPIO 4/5
are logged before any transfer (idle I2C is high), and the pin config is only changed when
the function is not qup1 (0130 dropped the pull-up).

--- a/bsd/dev/spes_amp.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/spes_amp.c
@@ -28,8 +28,9 @@
 #define AMP_RCG         0x1f278u        /* QUP0 S1 CMD; CFG +4, branch -4 */
 #define AMP_SE_PA       0x04a84000u
 /*
- * SE1's SDA/SCL are GPIO 4/5 with function qup1 (live DT qupv3_se1_i2c_active, 2 mA, no
- * bias); left as plain GPIOs every chip NACKed (all12). Same tile and function number as the
+ * SE1's SDA/SCL are GPIO 4/5 with function qup1 (live DT qupv3_se1_i2c_active). They already
+ * read 0x207 (function 1, pull-up) and every chip still NACKed (all12, all13), so the function
+ * is set only if it is not 1 and the pull-up is kept. Same tile and function number as the
  * touch driver's qup2 pins GPIO 6/7 (WEST 0x500000, mux 1).
  */
 #define AMP_WEST_PA     0x00500000u
@@ -242,18 +243,25 @@
